meta {
  name: admin - trigger entry rematch
  type: http
  seq: 64
}

post {
  url: {{bff_url}}/api/admin/rematch
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 202
  res.body.status: eq started
}

docs {
  Relays to collection's POST /internal/rematch-entries (admin-or-service
  guarded); collection answers 202 and detaches. The three counts - triples
  seen, triples failed, entries repointed - do not ride this response; they
  land in collection's "rematch-entries complete" log line and the
  vg.collection.rematch.* metrics instead. Rides the admin cookie left
  behind by ack-cleanup-login-admin.bru; the resnapshot relay (seq 65)
  closes the folder on the same cookie.

  No conflict sibling (unlike refresh-conflict.bru): the dev rematch
  dataset resolves in single-digit milliseconds, faster than two
  sequential HTTP calls can race it, so a second trigger here would
  flake between 202 and 409 rather than reliably proving the lock. The
  single-flight 409 is pinned instead by collection's own
  TestInternalRematchEntries_ConcurrentTriggerIs409 and the bff
  relay's TestUnitAdminRematch_ConflictRelaysVerbatim /
  TestTriggerRematch_ConflictIsRelayed unit tests.
}
